{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "def find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum number of rotations (greater than 0) to get the original string back.\n    This is equivalent to finding the smallest period length of the string.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    # The string concatenated with itself will contain all rotations of the original string.\n    # We search for the first occurrence of the original string starting from the second character.\n    # The index of this first occurrence is the minimum number of rotations.\n    doubled_s = s + s\n    return doubled_s.find(s, 1)"}
