{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "def comb_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements in ascending order using the comb sort algorithm.\n    It modifies the input list in-place and returns the sorted list.\"\"\"\n\n    def _get_next_gap(gap: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the next gap value for the comb sort algorithm using a shrink factor.\"\"\"\n        gap = (gap * 10) // 13\n        if gap < 1:\n            return 1\n        return gap\n\n    def _swap(arr_local: list, i: int, j: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Swaps two elements in the list at the given indices.\"\"\"\n        arr_local[i], arr_local[j] = arr_local[j], arr_local[i]\n\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Initialize gap size and set swapped to true to enter the loop\n    gap = n\n    swapped = True\n\n    # Keep running while gap is not 1 and a swap occurred in the last iteration\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        # Calculate the next gap value\n        gap = _get_next_gap(gap)\n\n        # Reset swapped flag for this pass\n        swapped = False\n\n        # Compare all elements with the current gap and swap if necessary\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                _swap(arr, i, i + gap)\n                swapped = True\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/72", "solution": "```python\ndef dif_Square(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number can be represented as the difference of two squares.\n    A number can be represented as a difference of two squares if it is not of the form 4k+2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        # A negative number -n can be represented as difference of squares if -n is not of form 4k+2\n        # For example, -5 = 2^2 - 3^2\n        # So we check the absolute value.\n        n = abs(n)\n    return n % 4 != 2\n```"}
