{"task_id": "Mbpp/87", "solution": "def merge_dictionaries_three(dict1: dict, dict2: dict, dict3: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Merges three dictionaries into a single dictionary, preserving the value from the first\n    dictionary encountered if a key exists in multiple inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    merged_dict = {}\n\n    # Iterate through dict1 first, adding all its items\n    for key, value in dict1.items():\n        merged_dict[key] = value\n\n    # Iterate through dict2, adding items only if the key is not already in merged_dict\n    for key, value in dict2.items():\n        if key not in merged_dict:\n            merged_dict[key] = value\n\n    # Iterate through dict3, adding items only if the key is not already in merged_dict\n    for key, value in dict3.items():\n        if key not in merged_dict:\n            merged_dict[key] = value\n\n    return merged_dict"}
