{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given positive integer is an undulating number.\n    An undulating number alternates between exactly two different digits and has at least 3 digits.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _extract_digits(num: int) -> list:\n        # Converts an integer to a list of its individual digits.\n        return [int(d) for d in str(num)]\n\n    def _validate_minimum_length(digits_list: list) -> bool:\n        # Checks if the digit list meets the minimum length requirement (at least 3).\n        return len(digits_list) >= 3\n\n    def _count_unique_digits(digits_list: list) -> int:\n        # Counts the number of unique digits present in the list.\n        return len(set(digits_list))\n\n    def _check_alternating_pattern(digits_list: list) -> bool:\n        # Validates if the sequence of digits alternates consistently between two distinct digits.\n        if len(digits_list) < 2:\n            return False\n\n        # The unique_digit_count check ensures there are exactly two unique digits.\n        # Here we only need to verify the pattern.\n        first_digit = digits_list[0]\n        second_digit = digits_list[1]\n\n        # If the number has exactly two unique digits and starts with two identical digits (e.g., 112),\n        # it cannot be undulating, but this case will be caught below if `first_digit == second_digit`.\n        # However, _count_unique_digits = 2 already implies d1 != d2 for the primary alternating pair.\n        # This check is mainly for structural alternation.\n        if first_digit == second_digit: # Example: 111, 1121 - if count_unique_digits is 2, this path shouldn't be hit with valid d1, d2\n             # If unique_digit_count is 2, then first_digit and second_digit *must* be different\n             # unless the number is very short (e.g., 12) where this function wouldn't be called directly.\n             # If d1 == d2, it means the count_unique_digits check for 2 would have failed or the pattern is 1121 (not undulating).\n             return False\n\n\n        for i in range(2, len(digits_list)):\n            if i % 2 == 0:  # Even index (0, 2, 4...) should match first_digit\n                if digits_list[i] != first_digit:\n                    return False\n            else:  # Odd index (1, 3, 5...) should match second_digit\n                if digits_list[i] != second_digit:\n                    return False\n        return True\n\n    digits = _extract_digits(number)\n\n    if not _validate_minimum_length(digits):\n        return False\n\n    unique_digit_count = _count_unique_digits(digits)\n    if unique_digit_count != 2:\n        return False\n\n    return _check_alternating_pattern(digits)"}
