{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "def next_smallest_palindrome(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the next smallest palindrome strictly greater than the input integer n.\n    It leverages nested helper functions for string manipulation and palindrome checking.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to reverse a string.\n    def reverse_string(s: str) -> str:\n        return s[::-1]\n\n    # Helper function to convert an integer to its string representation.\n    def int_to_string(num: int) -> str:\n        return str(num)\n\n    # Helper function to convert a string to its integer representation.\n    def string_to_int(s: str) -> int:\n        return int(s)\n\n    # Helper function to check if a number is a palindrome.\n    def is_palindrome(num: int) -> bool:\n        s = int_to_string(num)\n        return s == reverse_string(s)\n\n    # Helper function to iteratively find the next palindrome starting from num + 1.\n    def increment_and_check(num: int) -> int:\n        current_num = num + 1\n        while True:\n            if is_palindrome(current_num):\n                return current_num\n            current_num += 1\n\n    # Helper function implementing the core algorithm to find the next palindrome.\n    def find_next_palindrome(start_num: int) -> int:\n        return increment_and_check(start_num)\n\n    return find_next_palindrome(n)"}
