{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def sum(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of common divisors of two given numbers.\n    Orchestrates calls to helper functions for divisor calculation and summation.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def calculate_divisors(number: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates all divisors of a given number, including 1 and itself.\"\"\"\n        divs = []\n        for i in range(1, number + 1):\n            if number % i == 0:\n                divs.append(i)\n        return divs\n\n    def find_common_divisors(divisors1: list[int], divisors2: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Identifies divisors that are common to both input lists.\"\"\"\n        return list(set(divisors1) & set(divisors2))\n\n    def sum_divisors(divs: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all divisors in the provided list.\"\"\"\n        return builtins.sum(divs)\n\n    divisors_num1 = calculate_divisors(num1)\n    divisors_num2 = calculate_divisors(num2)\n    \n    common_divs = find_common_divisors(divisors_num1, divisors_num2)\n    \n    return sum_divisors(common_divs)"}
