{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number can be represented as a sum of distinct non-zero powers of 2.\n    This implementation follows the design context by performing explicit validation, power generation, and a greedy subset sum check.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Input Validation: Ensure the number is a positive integer.\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    # 2. Powers of Two Generation: Generate non-zero powers of 2 (2^1, 2^2, ...) up to the given number.\n    powers = []\n    current_power = 2  # Start with 2^1 (non-zero power)\n    while current_power <= number:\n        powers.append(current_power)\n        current_power *= 2\n\n    # 3. Sum Representation Check: Use a greedy algorithm (subset sum for distinct powers of 2)\n    # to see if the number can be formed by summing distinct powers from the generated list.\n    remaining_target = number\n    # Iterate through powers in descending order for the greedy approach\n    for power in reversed(powers):\n        if remaining_target >= power:\n            remaining_target -= power\n        if remaining_target == 0:\n            return True  # Found a valid sum representation\n\n    # If after checking all powers, the remaining target is 0, it means a sum was found.\n    return remaining_target == 0"}
