{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements using the pancake sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to reverse elements from 0 to i\n    def _flip(sub_arr, i):\n        start = 0\n        while start < i:\n            sub_arr[start], sub_arr[i] = sub_arr[i], sub_arr[start]\n            start += 1\n            i -= 1\n        return sub_arr\n\n    # Helper function to find the index of the maximum element in a given range\n    def _find_max_index(sub_arr, n):\n        max_element = sub_arr[0]\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, n):\n            if sub_arr[i] > max_element:\n                max_element = sub_arr[i]\n                max_idx = i\n        return max_idx\n\n    n = len(arr)\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current unsorted sub-array\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(arr, current_size)\n\n        # Move the maximum element to the beginning of the sub-array if it's not already there\n        if max_idx != 0:\n            _flip(arr, max_idx)\n\n        # Move the maximum element from the beginning to its correct position at the end of the current sub-array\n        _flip(arr, current_size - 1)\n    return arr"}
