{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "def find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Solves the linear Diophantine equation ax + by = n for integers x and y.\n    Returns (x, y) if a solution exists, otherwise returns None.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def gcd(a_val: int, b_val: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the greatest common divisor using the Euclidean algorithm.\"\"\"\n        while b_val:\n            a_val, b_val = b_val, a_val % b_val\n        return a_val\n\n    def extended_gcd(a_val: int, b_val: int) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Implements the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find gcd and coefficients.\"\"\"\n        if a_val == 0:\n            return b_val, 0, 1\n        \n        gcd_val, x1, y1 = extended_gcd(b_val % a_val, a_val)\n        x = y1 - (b_val // a_val) * x1\n        y = x1\n        return gcd_val, x, y\n\n    # Handle cases where a or b is zero\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        if n == 0:\n            return (0, 0) # Any (x, y) works, return (0,0) as a valid solution\n        else:\n            return None # 0 * x + 0 * y = n, impossible if n is not 0\n    \n    # Calculate gcd of a and b\n    common_divisor = gcd(abs(a), abs(b))\n\n    # If n is not divisible by common_divisor, no integer solution exists\n    if n % common_divisor != 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Find a particular solution (x_p, y_p) for a * x_p + b * y_p = common_divisor\n    g, x_p, y_p = extended_gcd(a, b)\n    \n    # Scale the particular solution to solve a * x + b * y = n\n    # We know n = k * g, so we need to multiply x_p, y_p by k = n / g\n    k = n // g\n    x = x_p * k\n    y = y_p * k\n\n    return (x, y)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/161", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_elements(source_list: list, removal_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes all elements from the source_list that are present in the removal_list.\n    Returns a new list with the remaining elements, preserving their original order.\n    \"\"\"\n    filtered_list = []\n    # Convert removal_list to a set for O(1) average time complexity lookups\n    removal_set = set(removal_list)\n    for element in source_list:\n        if element not in removal_set:\n            filtered_list.append(element)\n    return filtered_list\n```"}
