{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "def find_even_pair(integers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs of integers that XOR to an even number.\n    It identifies pairs (a,b) where a ^ b results in an even number.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def calculate_xor(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes XOR of two integers.\"\"\"\n        return a ^ b\n\n    def is_even(value: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if integer is even.\"\"\"\n        return (value % 2 == 0)\n\n    def generate_unique_pairs(data: list[int]) -> Iterator[tuple[int, int]]:\n        \"\"\"Generates unique pairs from integer list without self-pairing.\"\"\"\n        n_data = len(data)\n        for i in range(n_data):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n_data):\n                yield (data[i], data[j])\n\n    count = 0\n    for num1, num2 in generate_unique_pairs(integers):\n        xor_result = calculate_xor(num1, num2)\n        if is_even(xor_result):\n            count += 1\n\n    return count"}
