{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of set bits (binary digits with value 1) in a given number.\n    This implementation uses Brian Kernighan's algorithm for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    while number > 0:\n        number &= (number - 1)  # Clear the least significant set bit\n        count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to validate if the given length n matches the array's actual length.\n    def _validate_input(arr, length):\n        return len(arr) == length\n\n    # Helper function using modified binary search to find the index of the first occurrence of the target.\n    def _find_first_occurrence(arr, target):\n        low = 0\n        high = len(arr) - 1\n        first_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                first_idx = mid\n                high = mid - 1  # Search in the left half for an earlier occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > target\n                high = mid - 1\n        return first_idx\n\n    # Helper function using modified binary search to find the index of the last occurrence of the target.\n    def _find_last_occurrence(arr, target):\n        low = 0\n        high = len(arr) - 1\n        last_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                last_idx = mid\n                low = mid + 1  # Search in the right half for a later occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > target\n                high = mid - 1\n        return last_idx\n\n    # Validate the input array length against the provided n.\n    if not _validate_input(array, n):\n        return False\n\n    # Handle the case of an empty array.\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Find the first and last occurrences of the element using binary search.\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(array, element)\n    \n    # If the element is not found, it cannot be a majority element.\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(array, element)\n\n    # Calculate the total count of the element.\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    # Check if the count is greater than n/2.\n    return count > n / 2"}
