{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of possible sequences of length n,\n    where each element is a positive integer, is greater than or equal to twice the previous element,\n    and is less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _dp_recursive(current_idx: int, prev_val: int) -> int:\n        # Base case: If we have placed 'n' elements, one valid sequence is found.\n        if current_idx == n:\n            return 1\n\n        # Return memoized result if available.\n        if (current_idx, prev_val) in memo:\n            return memo[(current_idx, prev_val)]\n\n        count = 0\n        # Determine the minimum possible value for the current element.\n        # The first element must be at least 1; subsequent elements must be at least twice the previous.\n        min_current_val = 1 if current_idx == 0 else 2 * prev_val\n\n        # Iterate through all valid values for the current element.\n        for current_val in range(min_current_val, m + 1):\n            count += _dp_recursive(current_idx + 1, current_val)\n\n        # Store the computed result in the memoization table.\n        memo[(current_idx, prev_val)] = count\n        return count\n\n    # Start the recursive process from the first element (index 0) with an initial previous value of 0.\n    return _dp_recursive(0, 0)"}
