{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of possible sequences of length n.\n    Each element must be a positive integer, greater than or equal to twice the previous element, and less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {} # Memoization table to store results of subproblems.\n\n    def _count_sequences_dp(last_element: int, length_remaining: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursive helper to count sequences given the last placed element and remaining length.\n        \"\"\"\n        if length_remaining == 0:\n            return 1 # Base case: a valid sequence of the required length has been formed.\n\n        if (last_element, length_remaining) in memo:\n            return memo[(last_element, length_remaining)]\n\n        total_sequences_for_this_path = 0\n        min_next_val = last_element * 2\n\n        # Iterate through possible values for the next element in the sequence.\n        for next_val in range(min_next_val, m + 1):\n            total_sequences_for_this_path += _count_sequences_dp(next_val, length_remaining - 1)\n\n        memo[(last_element, length_remaining)] = total_sequences_for_this_path\n        return total_sequences_for_this_path\n\n    total_overall_sequences = 0\n    # For the first element (s_1) of the sequence, it can be any positive integer from 1 to m.\n    for s_1 in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_overall_sequences += _count_sequences_dp(s_1, n - 1)\n\n    return total_overall_sequences"}
