{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence using dynamic programming.\"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the LPS of substring s[i...j]\n    # Initialize with zeros.\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Base case: A single character is an LPS of length 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for substrings of increasing length.\n    # 'length' iterates from 2 up to n (inclusive).\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        # 'i' is the starting index of the substring.\n        # It goes from 0 up to n - length.\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1  # 'j' is the ending index of the substring.\n\n            # If the characters at the ends of the current substring s[i...j] match.\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # These two characters form part of the palindrome.\n                # The length is 2 plus the LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i+1][j-1]\n            else:\n                # If the characters do not match, take the maximum of\n                # LPS of s[i+1...j] (excluding s[i]) and LPS of s[i...j-1] (excluding s[j]).\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    # The result is the length of the LPS for the entire string s[0...n-1].\n    return dp[0][n-1]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    This is solved using dynamic programming by building up solutions for substrings.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # dp[i][j] will store the length of the LPS for substring s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromic subsequences of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for substrings of length 2 to n\n    # 'cl' is current length of the substring\n    for cl in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - cl + 1):\n            j = i + cl - 1  # 'j' is the ending index of the current substring\n\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters at ends match, they contribute 2 to LPS\n                # plus the LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1]\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                # If characters at ends don't match, take the maximum\n                # of LPS found by excluding s[i] or s[j]\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    # The result for the entire string s[0...n-1] is stored at dp[0][n-1]\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
