{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A bitonic subsequence is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # Calculate lis_sums: maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index i.\n    lis_sums = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        lis_sums[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lis_sums[i] = max(lis_sums[i], arr[i] + lis_sums[j])\n\n    # Calculate lds_sums: maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at index i.\n    lds_sums = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        lds_sums[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lds_sums[i] = max(lds_sums[i], arr[i] + lds_sums[j])\n\n    # Find the maximum bitonic sum. The peak element arr[i] is counted once.\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
