{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers strictly less than the given non-negative number.\n    Returns 0 if the input number is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _validate_input(n):\n        \"\"\"Checks if the given number is non-negative.\"\"\"\n        return n >= 0\n\n    def _is_prime(n):\n        \"\"\"Determines if a given number is prime using trial division.\"\"\"\n        if n < 2:\n            return False\n        if n == 2:\n            return True\n        if n % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= n:\n            if n % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    if not _validate_input(number):\n        return 0\n\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(2, number):\n        if _is_prime(i):\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
