{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "from typing import List, Any\n\ndef list_split(input_list: List[Any], n: int) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list into n sublists, distributing elements using modular arithmetic.\n    Each sublist contains elements at indices i, i+n, i+2n, etc., for a starting offset i.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer greater than 0\")\n\n    sublists = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    for i, element in enumerate(input_list):\n        sublist_index = i % n\n        sublists[sublist_index].append(element)\n\n    return sublists"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "```python\ndef list_split(input_list, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits an input list into n sublists, where each sublist contains every nth element\n    starting from different offsets.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        # Per design, no error handling for edge cases.\n        # However, for a functional implementation, n=0 or negative n would lead to issues.\n        # Assuming n will always be a positive integer based on requirements.\n        return [[]] * (0 if n <= 0 else n) # Return empty lists based on n for consistency, though per instructions no error handling/checks.\n\n    result = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    for i, element in enumerate(input_list):\n        target_sublist_index = i % n\n        result[target_sublist_index].append(element)\n\n    return result\n```"}
