{"task_id": "Mbpp/274", "solution": "def even_binomial_Coeff_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of even-indexed binomial coefficients C(n,k) where k is even, by direct computation.\n    This implementation follows the detailed component breakdown provided in the design context.\"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to compute factorial(val) for non-negative integer val.\n    def _factorial(val: int) -> int:\n        res = 1\n        for i in range(1, val + 1):\n            res *= i\n        return res\n\n    # Helper function to compute the binomial coefficient C(n_val, k_val).\n    def _calculate_binomial_coefficient(n_val: int, k_val: int) -> int:\n        # Given that n is a positive integer and k iterates from 0 to n,\n        # k_val and (n_val - k_val) will always be non-negative.\n        return _factorial(n_val) // (_factorial(k_val) * _factorial(n_val - k_val))\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Iterate through even indices k from 0 up to and including n.\n    for k in range(0, n + 1, 2):\n        total_sum += _calculate_binomial_coefficient(n, k)\n\n    return total_sum"}
