{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(array, length, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous array in the modified array formed by\n    repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle edge cases for empty array or no repetitions.\n    if length == 0 or k == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Helper function: Kadane's Algorithm for maximum subarray sum\n    def kadane_algorithm(arr):\n        # Initializes max_so_far and current_max_running to the first element's value.\n        # This correctly handles arrays with all negative numbers.\n        max_so_far = arr[0]\n        current_max_running = arr[0]\n\n        for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n            current_max_running = max(arr[i], current_max_running + arr[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max_running)\n        return max_so_far\n\n    # Helper function: Calculate the sum of all elements in the array\n    def calculate_array_sum(arr):\n        return sum(arr)\n\n    # If the array is repeated only once, a simple Kadane's algorithm is sufficient.\n    if k == 1:\n        return kadane_algorithm(array)\n\n    # For k > 1, we consider the sum of the original array and a doubled version.\n    arr_sum = calculate_array_sum(array)\n    doubled_array = array + array\n    \n    # Calculate the maximum subarray sum in the doubled array.\n    # This covers cases where the max subarray spans across the boundary of two blocks.\n    max_sum_two_blocks = kadane_algorithm(doubled_array)\n\n    # If the total sum of the original array is positive,\n    # then repeating it further will potentially increase the maximum sum.\n    # The (k-2) middle blocks would contribute (k-2) * arr_sum to the total.\n    if arr_sum > 0:\n        return max_sum_two_blocks + (k - 2) * arr_sum\n    else:\n        # If the total sum is zero or negative,\n        # additional full repetitions (beyond the two already considered)\n        # would not increase the maximum sum (or would decrease it).\n        # Thus, the maximum sum will be found within the first two repetitions.\n        return max_sum_two_blocks"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/290", "solution": "def max_length(input_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the list of maximum length in a list of lists and returns its length and the list itself.\n    Returns the first occurrence if multiple lists have the same maximum length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_lists:\n        return (0, [])\n\n    max_len = 0\n    max_list = []\n\n    for current_list in input_lists:\n        current_len = len(current_list)\n        if current_len > max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n            max_list = current_list\n            \n    return (max_len, max_list)"}
