{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, length, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in an array repeated k times.\n    The length parameter is unused as Python lists provide their length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k == 0:\n        return 0\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    # Helper Kadane's function to find max subarray sum in a single array.\n    # Assumes non-empty array and returns max sum of a non-empty subarray.\n    def kadane(nums):\n        current_max = nums[0]\n        global_max = nums[0]\n        for x in nums[1:]:\n            current_max = max(x, current_max + x)\n            global_max = max(global_max, current_max)\n        return global_max\n\n    # 1. Calculate max sum for a single repetition of the array.\n    # This also serves as the initial `res` for comparisons.\n    res = kadane(arr)\n\n    # If k is 1, we just return the result from a single array.\n    if k == 1:\n        return res\n\n    # 2. For k > 1, further calculations are needed.\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n\n    # Calculate the maximum sum of any prefix of the original array.\n    current_prefix_sum = 0\n    max_prefix_sum = -float('inf')\n    for x in arr:\n        current_prefix_sum += x\n        max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, current_prefix_sum)\n\n    # Calculate the maximum sum of any suffix of the original array.\n    current_suffix_sum = 0\n    max_suffix_sum = -float('inf')\n    for x in reversed(arr):\n        current_suffix_sum += x\n        max_suffix_sum = max(max_suffix_sum, current_suffix_sum)\n\n    # The maximum sum could occur entirely within the first two array repetitions,\n    # or span across their boundary. This is found by applying Kadane's to `arr + arr`.\n    res = max(res, kadane(arr + arr))\n\n    # If the total sum of the array is positive and k is greater than 2,\n    # it might be optimal to include full array blocks in the middle.\n    if total_sum > 0 and k > 2:\n        # The maximum sum could be formed by a max suffix from the first block,\n        # plus (k-2) full total_sum blocks, plus a max prefix from the last block.\n        res = max(res, max_suffix_sum + (k - 2) * total_sum + max_prefix_sum)\n\n    return res"}
