{"task_id": "Mbpp/294", "solution": "def max_val(heterogeneous_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum numeric value in a given heterogeneous list.\n    Non-numeric elements are ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _filter_numeric_values(input_list):\n        \"\"\"Filters out non-numeric values from the input list.\"\"\"\n        return [item for item in input_list if isinstance(item, (int, float))]\n\n    def _find_maximum(numeric_list):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the maximum value from a list of numeric values.\"\"\"\n        if not numeric_list:\n            return None # Or raise an error, but requirements say no exceptions.\n        return max(numeric_list)\n\n    numeric_values = _filter_numeric_values(heterogeneous_list)\n    return _find_maximum(numeric_values)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/293", "solution": "import math\n\ndef otherside_rightangle(side1, side2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the hypotenuse given two legs of a right-angled triangle.\n    This function assumes the two input sides are the legs of the triangle.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Using the Pythagorean theorem: a^2 + b^2 = c^2, where c is the hypotenuse.\n    # Here, side1 and side2 are treated as the legs (a and b).\n    hypotenuse_squared = side1**2 + side2**2\n    return math.sqrt(hypotenuse_squared)"}
