{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "def large_product(list1: list, list2: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the specified number of largest products from two given lists.\n    Selects one factor from each list and returns products in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _validate_inputs(lst1: list, lst2: list, num: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates input lists and count parameter for correctness.\"\"\"\n        if not lst1 or not lst2:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input lists cannot be empty.\")\n        if not all(isinstance(x, (int, float)) for x in lst1) or \\\n           not all(isinstance(x, (int, float)) for x in lst2):\n            raise ValueError(\"Input lists must contain only numeric values.\")\n        if not isinstance(num, int) or num <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n        if num > len(lst1) * len(lst2):\n            raise ValueError(\"n cannot be greater than the total number of possible products.\")\n\n    def _calculate_all_products(lst1: list, lst2: list) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Generates all possible products by multiplying one element from each list.\"\"\"\n        products = []\n        for x in lst1:\n            for y in lst2:\n                products.append(x * y)\n        return products\n\n    def _get_top_n_products(products_list: list, num: int) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Sorts products in descending order and returns the top n largest values.\"\"\"\n        products_list.sort(reverse=True)\n        return products_list[:num]\n\n    _validate_inputs(list1, list2, n)\n    all_products = _calculate_all_products(list1, list2)\n    return _get_top_n_products(all_products, n)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(array, length, i, k):\n    # If i is negative, no prefix elements are considered; the sum is just array[k].\n    if i < 0:\n        return array[k]\n\n    # Calculate Maximum Sum Increasing Subsequence (MSIS) for the prefix up to index i.\n    msis_prefix_sums = [array[p] for p in range(i + 1)]\n\n    # Fill the dp array using dynamic programming.\n    for p in range(i + 1):\n        for q in range(p):\n            if array[p] > array[q]:\n                msis_prefix_sums[p] = max(msis_prefix_sums[p], msis_prefix_sums[q] + array[p])\n\n    # Find the maximum sum that includes array[k].\n    # Initialize with array[k] to cover cases where no valid prefix subsequence exists.\n    max_overall_sum = array[k]\n\n    # Iterate through prefix sums to find the best preceding subsequence for array[k].\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if array[j] < array[k]:\n            max_overall_sum = max(max_overall_sum, msis_prefix_sums[j] + array[k])\n\n    return max_overall_sum"}
