{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n'th Lucas number using an iterative approach.\n    The sequence starts with L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(n) = L(n-1) + L(n-2).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        a, b = 2, 1  # L(0), L(1)\n        for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n            next_lucas = a + b\n            a = b\n            b = next_lucas\n        return b"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n'th Lucas number using an iterative approach.\n    The Lucas sequence starts with L(0)=2 and L(1)=1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        # Per design, assume valid positive integer input or handle it implicitly.\n        # This implementation aligns with the iterative calculation for non-negative n.\n        pass\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    \n    a, b = 2, 1  # L(0), L(1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b  # L(k-1), L(k)\n    return b"}
