{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "_memo = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum using the recursive equation f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Uses memoization to optimize performance for overlapping subproblems.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n    \n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n    \n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n: int, memo: dict = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum using the recursive equation f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Memoization is used to optimize performance by storing results of subproblems.\n    \"\"\"\n    if memo is None:\n        memo = {}\n\n    if n in memo:\n        return memo[n]\n\n    # Base case: For n=0, the sum of its parts is 0, so max(0, 0) is 0.\n    # For small n, the max(..., n) ensures termination if n is greater than the sum of its parts.\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Recursive step with integer division\n    sum_of_parts = get_max_sum(n // 2, memo) + \\\n                   get_max_sum(n // 3, memo) + \\\n                   get_max_sum(n // 4, memo) + \\\n                   get_max_sum(n // 5, memo)\n\n    # Apply the maximum condition from the equation\n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n\n    # Store the result in the memoization cache before returning\n    memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
