{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of all individual digits from numbers in a given list.\n    Handles multi-digit numbers, single-digit numbers, and negative numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n\n    def _get_absolute_value(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Converts a number to its absolute value.\"\"\"\n        return abs(number)\n\n    def _extract_digits(number: int) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Extracts individual digits from a single number.\"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return [0]\n        digits = []\n        while number > 0:\n            digits.append(number % 10)\n            number //= 10\n        return digits[::-1] # Reverse to maintain original digit order, though not strictly necessary for sum\n\n    for number in numbers:\n        absolute_number = _get_absolute_value(number)\n        digit_list = _extract_digits(absolute_number)\n        total_sum += sum(digit_list)\n\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def _extract_digits(number: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract individual digits from a number.\n    Converts the number to a string and then to a list of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    return [int(d) for d in str(number)]\n\ndef _sum_individual_digits(digits: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sum a list of individual digits.\n    This simply sums all elements in the given list.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum(digits)\n\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the sum of all individual digits from numbers in the input list.\n    It iterates through each number, extracts its digits, and sums them up.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum_of_all_digits = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        digits = _extract_digits(number)\n        total_sum_of_all_digits += _sum_individual_digits(digits)\n    return total_sum_of_all_digits"}
