{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts an array using the Shell sort algorithm with Knuth's gap sequence.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return arr[:] # Return a copy for immutability\n\n    # Array Copy Utility: Create a new array without modifying original\n    arr_copy = arr[:]\n\n    # Gap Sequence Generator: Generate decreasing gap values using Knuth's formula\n    gaps = []\n    h = 1\n    while h < n / 3:\n        h = 3 * h + 1\n    while h >= 1:\n        gaps.append(h)\n        h //= 3\n\n    # Core sorting logic: Perform insertion sort with each gap\n    for gap in gaps:\n        # Insertion Sort with Gap\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr_copy[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and arr_copy[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr_copy[j] = arr_copy[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr_copy[j] = temp\n\n    return arr_copy"}
