{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\n    This means summing the first n+1 terms of the Perrin sequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        return 0  # Perrin numbers are defined for non-negative indices.\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 3\n    if n == 1:\n        return 3  # P(0) + P(1) = 3 + 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 5  # P(0) + P(1) + P(2) = 3 + 0 + 2\n\n    perrin_sequence = [3, 0, 2]\n    current_sum = 5  # Sum of P(0), P(1), P(2)\n\n    # Generate subsequent Perrin numbers P(3) through P(n)\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        next_perrin = perrin_sequence[i - 2] + perrin_sequence[i - 3]\n        perrin_sequence.append(next_perrin)\n        current_sum += next_perrin\n\n    return current_sum"}
