{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) up to P(n).\"\"\"\n    # Determine the total number of Perrin numbers to generate.\n    # To sum up to P(n), we need n+1 numbers (P(0), P(1), ..., P(n)).\n    count_to_generate = n + 1\n\n    # Inlined logic inspired by generate_perrin_sequence\n    if count_to_generate <= 0:\n        perrin_sequence = []\n    elif count_to_generate == 1:\n        perrin_sequence = [3]  # P(0)\n    elif count_to_generate == 2:\n        perrin_sequence = [3, 0] # P(0), P(1)\n    else:\n        perrin_sequence = [3, 0, 2]  # P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2\n        # Generate subsequent Perrin numbers using the recurrence P(i) = P(i-2) + P(i-3)\n        for i in range(3, count_to_generate):\n            next_val = perrin_sequence[i-2] + perrin_sequence[i-3]\n            perrin_sequence.append(next_val)\n\n    # Inlined logic inspired by calculate_sum\n    return sum(perrin_sequence)"}
