{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def normalize_tuple(t: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Convert tuple to normalized form (min, max) for comparison.\"\"\"\n    return tuple(sorted(t))\n\ndef find_matches(normalized_tuple: tuple, tuple_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Find all tuples in tuple_list that match the given normalized form.\"\"\"\n    matches = []\n    for t_item in tuple_list:\n        if normalize_tuple(t_item) == normalized_tuple:\n            matches.append(t_item)\n    return matches\n\ndef tuple_intersection(list1: list, list2: list) -> set:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find intersection of two tuple lists treating tuples as order-independent.\n    Returns a set of original tuples from list1 that have an equivalent in list2.\n    \"\"\"\n    intersection_set = set()\n    for t1 in list1:\n        normalized_t1 = normalize_tuple(t1)\n        # Use find_matches to check if an equivalent tuple exists in list2\n        if find_matches(normalized_t1, list2):\n            intersection_set.add(t1)\n    return intersection_set"}
