{"task_id": "Mbpp/736", "solution": "def left_insertion(array: list, target_value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the left insertion point for a specified value in a sorted array.\n    Uses binary search to find the index where the target can be inserted\n    to maintain sorted order, ensuring the leftmost position for duplicates.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n    # 'ans' stores the potential insertion point. Initialize to len(array)\n    # in case the target is greater than all elements.\n    ans = len(array)\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] >= target_value:\n            # Current mid is a possible answer. Try to find an even smaller index to its left.\n            ans = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        else:\n            # array[mid] is less than target, so target must be in the right half.\n            low = mid + 1\n            \n    return ans"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/736", "solution": "def left_insertion(array, target):\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the left insertion point for a specified value in a sorted array using binary search.\n    This function finds the first index 'i' such that all elements 'array[k]' for k < 'i' are less than 'target'.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n            \n    return low"}
