{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Rotate left bits by d bits for a 32-bit number, ensuring 32-bit wraparound.\"\"\"\n    BITS = 32\n    d = d % BITS  # Ensure rotation amount is within 0 to BITS-1\n    return ((number << d) | (number >> (BITS - d))) & (2**BITS - 1)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotate left bits by d bits for a 32-bit number.\n\n    Args:\n        number: 32-bit integer to rotate\n        d: Number of positions to rotate left\n\n    Returns:\n        32-bit integer with bits rotated left\n    \"\"\"\n    NUM_BITS = 32\n    # Normalize the rotation amount to be within 0 and NUM_BITS-1\n    normalized_d = d % NUM_BITS\n    # Create a 32-bit mask\n    mask = (1 << NUM_BITS) - 1\n\n    # Perform the left shift and combine with the bits that wrapped around\n    # Then apply the 32-bit mask to ensure the result is within 32 bits\n    return ((number << normalized_d) | (number >> (NUM_BITS - normalized_d))) & mask"}
